scalar-connection-c6237c1e.conceptual_definition:
The Einstein field equations (EFE) are a set of 10 coupled non-linear partial differential equations that describe the fundamental interaction of gravitation as a result of spacetime being curved by matter and energy. In this simplified form, the equation relates the curvature of spacetime, represented by the Einstein tensor (
    G_{\mu\nu}
), to the distribution of mass and energy, represented by the stress-energy tensor (
    T_{\mu\nu}
). The constants in front (
    8πG / c^4
) bridge the geometric aspect of gravity with the physical source of gravity.

